ce, and no clear financial or environmental edge for either side.\n\nThe Democratic field is still unsettled. Senator Jon Ossoff has drawn attention in early 2028 nomination polls and prediction markets, and polling has shown him competitive in his home state, but he has publicly disclaimed interest in running. Until a nominee emerges and Georgia-specific polling arrives, the race is best treated as a near coin flip with a slight Republican tilt and wide uncertainty about how either coalition will hold.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.4567, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.4683, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.467, "margin": -1.0}]}